  "label": "Monarchy as Symbol",
  "description": "The image of Queen Elizabeth II and Prince Charles is used to represent the British monarchy, which is a symbol of national unity and tradition. The meme uses this image to imply that the government (represented by the monarchy) is making absurd or overreaching decisions, which is a form of political satire. The use of the monarchy as a symbol is a common trope in political memes, as it evokes a sense of authority and tradition.",
